		<profileDesc>
			<abstract>
				<p>We introduce the first highly multilingual speech and American Sign Language (ASL) comprehension dataset by extending BELE-BELE. Our dataset covers 91 spoken languages at the intersection of BELEBELE and FLEURS, and one sign language (ASL). As a by-product we also extend the Automatic Speech Recognition Benchmark, FLEURS, by 20%. We evaluate 2M-BELEBELE dataset for both 5-shot and zero-shot settings and across languages, the speech comprehension accuracy is ≈ 10% average lower compared to reading comprehension.</p>
			</abstract>
